{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"grouchy-coexistent-snowgeese","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Six subsystem agents triaged every substantial comment in `src/rebar` (439 files) against the\nmaintainer's destination taxonomy: history belongs in tickets, architecture in ADRs, logic in code,\ncontracts in schema, and comments carry only proximate just-in-time context in concise language.\n\nTotal recoverable: **~2,033 lines**. Per shard: reconciler ~970, plan_review+workflow ~230,\nstore/reducer ~230, llm core ~218, commands/CLI ~205, root/services ~180.\n\nThe largest single category is self-referential: **prose explaining the 800-LOC cap**, occupying the\nbudget it describes. 28 sites in the reconciler alone carry variants of \"RELOCATED VERBATIM out of\ntransport.py; this module changes no behaviour. The move is forced by the LOCKED 800-line cap.\" The\nloop closes at `outbound_differ.py:164`, which records that a fix had to \"buy its lines back from\nreal duplication instead of from comments\" because the module sat at the cap.\n\nHeadroom recovered where it is tightest: `runner.py` 3 → ~48 lines (the repo's #1 hotspot, 88\ncommits, whose 371-line method sits at its C901 ceiling); `_ref_lock.py` 1 → ~21; `dispatch_one.py`\n14 → ~57; `inbound_differ.py` 18 → ~66; `fetcher.py` 29 → ~80.\n\nHonest counterweight, and it must not be lost: **comment triage cannot fix three files.**\n`_store/event_append.py` (791) recovers ~10 lines; `reducer/_processors.py` (777) recovers ~3;\n`signing.py` (798) recovers ~5-8. Their comments ARE the replay-compat and security invariants. Each\nshard identified the real call-graph seam instead, and those splits are out of scope here.\n\nEvery shard produced a `do_not_move` list — blocks that look relocatable but are load-bearing. Those\nlists are the protection record and must be preserved (appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md`) so a\nfuture sweep does not re-flag them. Examples: \"on DC 8.17.1 the `fields.parent` write answers HTTP\n204 and is silently ignored. Do not 'simplify' that extra round trip away\"; \"ACLI's `--out`/`--in`\nare INVERTED relative to the naive reading\"; \"READ FROM `exc.response.headers`, NOT `exc.headers`\".\n\nVerified-stale comments found along the way (correctness, not verbosity): six sites say the\ndeterministic floor is \"P1-P9\" while `DET_CHECKS` has 11 entries and runs P1..P11; three sites in\n`llm/` assert an Anthropic constraint that `structured.py:228-238` explicitly calls \"a stale\nrationale\" and \"a relic\" 210 lines below one of them; `_backend_registry.py:3` says \"STUB:\nsignatures pinned, bodies to be implemented\" while `select_backend` is imported by 13 modules;\n`_io/__init__.py:14` says the import side \"lands in a later sub-task\" six lines above the line that\nimports it; `reducer/llm_format.py:1-28` documents a key map that omits four keys present directly\nbelow it and cites a module path that does not exist.\n\n~13 new ADRs are proposed across the shards, each consolidating an argument currently restated 4-8\ntimes. The largest: \"one idempotent transform, applied fit-then-normalize, on the local side only\" —\nthe same four-paragraph argument at 8 sites, warning that \"Swapping the two re-introduces a diff\nthat never converges.\"\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All six shards complete, each landing separately\n- [ ] Each shard's `do_not_move` list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` before that shard's edits land\n- [ ] History that already cites a ticket is reduced to the citation; history citing none has a ticket filed first\n- [ ] Proposed ADRs are written and the inline blocks reduced to citations\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected, not deleted, where they document a live invariant\n- [ ] No file's comment density is reduced by deleting a load-bearing invariant","id":"373f-8c1d-cef0-41bf","parent_id":"b5bc-f4f7-3433-4181","priority":3,"tags":["janitor"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Comment triage: relocate history, rationale and contracts out of src"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786047042647536001,"uuid":"b6f02870-1ff0-46d0-ab2f-29eaa5876f53"}